---
// Draft: needs review by a legal professional before launch (the page says so).
// The only contact detail is the mobile number from site.ts.
import LegalPage from '../components/company/LegalPage.astro';
import { site, contact, href, contactHref } from '../data/site';

const sections = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', title: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'data-we-collect', title: 'Personal data we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use', title: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'consent', title: 'Consent' },
  { id: 'sharing', title: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'client-data', title: 'Data we process for clients' },
  { id: 'retention', title: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'How we protect it' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'cookies', title: 'Cookies' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects personal data, in line with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.`}
  updated="2 November 2026"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="who-we-are">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is run by us (“we”, “us”). For personal data we collect through this website, we are the <strong>Data Fiduciary</strong> under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (the “DPDP Act”).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-we-collect">
    <h2>2. Personal data we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name and mobile number, the topic you choose and any note you add.</li>
      <li><strong>Job applications:</strong> the details and links you choose to share.</li>
      <li><strong>Calls and messages:</strong> notes about an enquiry or project.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> what your browser sends when loading a page, such as IP address and browser type, which our hosting provider may log.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Please don’t send identity documents, passwords or financial details through the contact form.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use">
    <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to your enquiry and discuss a possible project.</li>
      <li>To assess job applications.</li>
      <li>To keep the website secure and working.</li>
      <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don’t sell personal data or use it for advertising.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="consent">
    <h2>4. Consent</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit the contact form, you consent to us using those details to respond to your enquiry. You can withdraw consent at any time through the <a href={contactHref('other')}>contact form</a>{contact.phone ? <> or by calling <a href={contact.phoneHref}>{contact.phone}</a></> : null}. Withdrawal doesn’t affect anything done before it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We share personal data only with service providers that help us run this website, acting on our instructions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Form delivery:</strong> Web3Forms, which delivers contact form messages to us.</li>
      <li><strong>Website hosting:</strong> GitHub Pages, which serves this website.</li>
      <li><strong>Professional advisers:</strong> accountants and lawyers, where needed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Fonts are served from this website itself. We may also disclose data where the law requires it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="client-data">
    <h2>6. Data we process for clients</h2>
    <p>
      When we build or run software for a client, such as a CRM, HRMS or lending tool, the client decides what personal data is processed and is the Data Fiduciary. We act as a Data Processor under our contract with them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep personal data as long as needed to respond to your enquiry, and as required by law.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>8. How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
      Access is limited to people who need it, and connections are encrypted (HTTPS). If a personal data breach occurs, we will notify the Data Protection Board of India and the people affected, as the DPDP Act requires.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights">
    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the DPDP Act, you can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask what personal data we hold about you;</li>
      <li>ask us to correct, update or erase it;</li>
      <li>nominate someone to act for you in case of death or incapacity;</li>
      <li>withdraw consent; and</li>
      <li>raise a grievance with us, and then with the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>10. Cookies</h2>
    <p>This website doesn’t use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions or requests about your personal data, {contact.phone
        ? <>call us on <a href={contact.phoneHref}>{contact.phone}</a> or use the <a href={contactHref()}>contact form</a>.</>
        : <>use the <a href={contactHref()}>contact form</a>.</>}
      See also our <a href={href('/terms/')}>terms of use</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
